TLP is a command-line tool for optimizing Linux laptop power
management. It applies power-saving settings automatically on
startup and when power sources change.

This package contains the core TLP tools, the TLP Profiles Daemon
(tlp-pd) with its client (tlpctl), and the Radio Device Wizard
(tlp-rdw).

The TLP Profiles Daemon provides the power-profiles daemon interface
without requiring power-profiles-daemon or systemd. The Radio Device
Wizard requires NetworkManager.
